.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_EXFAT 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_exfat
.Nd mount an exFAT file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Op Fl g Ar group
.Op Fl m Ar mask
.Ar special
.Ar node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
mounts the exFAT file system on the device
.Ar special
at the directory
.Ar node .
It is usually run by
.Xr mount 8
as
.Ql mount -t exfat ,
or by
.Xr diskarbitrationd 8
when an exFAT disk appears.
.Pp
The file system is mounted read only: this release of the exfat kernel
extension reads exFAT but does not write it.
.Pp
exFAT keeps no owner or permissions for its files. All of them take the
owner, group and permissions given by these options, or by default those of
.Ar node ;
with none of
.Fl u ,
.Fl g
and
.Fl m ,
as on macOS, the permissions are 0777 (how
.Xr diskarbitrationd 8
mounts a volume):
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl o Ar options
Options as in
.Xr mount 8 ,
such as
.Cm noexec .
.It Fl u Ar user
The owner of the files, a name or a number.
.It Fl g Ar group
The group of the files, a name or a number.
.It Fl m Ar mask
The permissions of the files, in octal.
.El
.Pp
Names are looked up without regard to case, with the volume's own up-case
table. Times saved with their offset from UTC are converted with it; the
others are taken as local time in the time zone in effect when the file
system is mounted.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Mount the first partition of a USB disk, owned by user
.Ql minkar :
.Pp
.Dl mount_exfat -u minkar /dev/disk2s1 /Volumes/USB
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount 2 ,
.Xr fsck_exfat 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr newfs_exfat 8
.Sh BUGS
Writing is not supported yet.
